@title Parental leave FAQ
@subtitle Policy effective 2026-11-01

Becoming a parent is a big change, and you should not have to dig for answers. This page covers the questions we hear most often. If yours is not here, ask us.

## How much leave do I get?

Primary caregivers get 16 weeks of leave at full pay. Secondary caregivers get 8 weeks at full pay. This is the same for birth, adoption and foster placement.

## Who is eligible?

You are eligible if you have worked at Tessellate for at least 6 months on the day your leave starts.

## When can I start and finish?

You can start up to 2 weeks before your expected date. You have to finish your leave within 12 months of the birth or placement.

## Can I split my leave?

Yes. You can take your leave in at most 2 blocks. Agree the second block with your manager at least 4 weeks ahead.

## What happens to my pay, benefits and equity?

You are paid full pay for your leave weeks. Health insurance continues at the normal employer contribution. Equity keeps vesting during your leave.

## How do I come back?

You can come back on a transition schedule. For the first 4 weeks, you work 80 percent of your time at 100 percent pay.

## How do I apply?

Tell your manager and the People Team at least 30 days ahead, through the leave form in the HR portal. If you are arriving early, tell us as soon as you can. Questions go to leave@tessellate.example or to the #people-help channel.
